# KEY|what it is and what the kit uses it for|where to get it|after (needed only after the first install)|when
MACHINE_ROLE|server: power settings so the Mac never sleeps and starts up again by itself after a power cut. laptop: power settings are left alone.|||
TIMEZONE|Used by every app for schedules and log times. Detected from this Mac.|||
MEDIA_ROOT|Where Downloads, Movies and TV Shows live. It can be on an external drive; app data stays on the internal disk either way.|||
MEDIA_SERVER|Streams your library to TVs, phones and browsers. Plex needs a free Plex account; Jellyfin needs no account. Both is fine.|||
BACKUP_DRIVE|Weekly backups always stay on this Mac; give a folder on an external drive (APFS recommended) to also copy them there whenever it's plugged in.|||
UPDATE_SCHEDULE|off: run update-all by hand. weekly: update every app once a week.|||
APPS_DIR|Where the kit installs native apps such as Plex. /Applications for everyone on this Mac; ~/Applications keeps them in this account (needed when this account isn't an admin). An app already in either place isn't installed again.|||
HOME_ROUTER|This Mac's usual router (its default gateway), filled in from the network at the first install. check-health warns when traffic goes through a different one. Empty: not checked.|||
HOST_TAILSCALE|Whether check-health watches the Tailscale app on this Mac itself. auto: only if it's installed.|||
